and in the wake of the most recent mass  shootings plaguing this country  survivors along with local and state  leaders are coming together to talk  about gun violence prevention thanks for  joining us here at six i'm denise valdez  and i'm brian loftis madison kimbrough  live in our newsroom with what was  discussed the topic is heavy but so  necessary right now and with it being  national gun violence awareness day  state leaders joined a group of  community members to discuss the  importance of gun laws and how we move  forward with plans to ensure our  community stay safe  it's not just in schools it's in  rec centers it's in  movie theaters it's at concerts it's at  libraries and medical centers and it's  it's got to change a plea from  democratic congressman stephen horsford  on the topic of gun violence as he and  congresswoman susie lee held a round  table discussion friday discussing the  need for stricter gun laws jamie bonnell  with the nevada chapter of moms demand  action for gun sense in america says as  a gun owner herself she and her family  believes more needs to be done to ensure  those with weapons are properly equipped  to handle them it doesn't bother me to  have background checks it doesn't bother  me to as a gun owner you know to wait a  little bit longer before i get the  weapon that i want to purchase  and i don't  i firmly believe that responsible gun  owners  also agree in that gina morano is also a  member of the organization and a one  october survivor she says with these  most recent shootings it brings back the  pain from that day nearly five years ago  i'm glad i'm grateful that i'm okay but  you forget how close to that you are and  it's really terrifying to then hear  about other people having to experience  it i think my anxiety now has just  really like gone to every situation  possible  because you never know following the  uvalde texas school shooting  congresswoman susie lee signed a letter  to house leadership calling for  immediate action to address gun violence  and the house is poised to vote on a  slate of gun violence prevention bills  next week  now in an hour that group nevada moms  demand action gun safety advocates will  host a unity wear orange event to honor  the lives of those affected by gun  violence it's at lorenzi park that's on  washington near rancho in the newsroom  madison kimbrough live local now
 

